  "osc_assignment_note": "osc[i] / CTRL sel i is this bench's convention; neither rtl/ nor spec/ fixes an osc[i]-to-oscillator assignment (sta/run_osc_sta.py records the same gap)",
  "phase_convention": "the oscillator's first rising edge is half an oscillator period after the clk_ref edge that samples the CTRL start write -- a fixed, reproducible mid-phase. When the gate window is shorter than one oscillator period, completion is phase-dependent (test_readout.py::k0_phase_sweep: a read hangs iff no rising edge lands inside the window), so this convention is part of the recorded result."
 },
